{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"review-plan (unsandboxed, 12:24-12:41 PST): verdict PASS, 0 blocking, advisories recorded. Acting on 2 after testing them: (a) an unusable proxy value (e.g. ALL_PROXY=ftp://...) makes AsyncHTTPTransport(proxy=...) raise ValueError at construction - httpx's own default client raises too, but rebar works today because it ignores the variable, so the routing transport will log a warning naming the variable's scheme (no URL, no credentials) and skip that proxy; (b) loopback hosts (rebar's existing _LOOPBACK_HOSTS set plus *.localhost) always connect directly, so a local OpenAI-compatible server keeps working when a proxy variable is set without NO_PROXY. Both get tests, written first. Not acting on: subclassing http_module.AsyncBaseTransport (the duck-typed transport already serves both modules; the httpx2 test passes), a DEBUG log of the resolved proxies, a neutral module for the helper (providers.py already imports from anthropic_model). The acceptance criteria are unchanged."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795380168364007001,"uuid":"7bfd0ea9-a4a5-4529-9545-3dd846ea5acd"}